  "title": "Odd Perfect Numbers",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Does there exist an odd perfect number? A perfect number is a positive integer that is equal to the sum of its proper divisors (excluding itself). For example, $6 = 1 + 2 + 3$ is perfect.",
